# The viewer rewrites its address to a public app route once an app is open; these routes serve viewer.html
# (a rewrite, status 200), so a reload or a shared link opens the same app. Same mapping as find3r.app.
# The target is the extensionless form: Pages serves every page without its .html and redirects the .html
# address to it, and a rewrite to viewer.html would be turned into that redirect, losing the route.
/app/* /viewer 200
/app-full/* /viewer 200
